{"data": [{"author_id": "1960171581847547904", "created_at": "2026-10-26T10:54:34.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114672027005014494"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/dnystedt/statu…", "end": 303, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/dnystedt/status/2114551864004166061", "start": 280, "url": "https://t.co/n73z7MbrD1"}]}, "id": "2114672027005014494", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 47, "impression_count": 37274, "like_count": 129, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 7, "retweet_count": 17}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2114551864004166061", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "While Nvidia beats sky-high expectations every quarter, China’s second-biggest AI chip designer’s Q3 revenue missed revenue expectations by a massive 44% due to capacity constraints and memory shortages. China’s AI chipmaking remains massively constrained due to export controls. https://t.co/n73z7MbrD1", "url": "https://x.com/ChrisRMcGuire/status/2114672027005014494"}, {"author_id": "1907851396168466433", "created_at": "2026-10-27T11:53:37.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115049274756985326"], "id": "2115049274756985326", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 13, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Taiwan is preparing to tighten AI-chip export controls. That is not diplomacy. It is a new approval layer between the fab and your contract. Taiwan makes 90% of advanced AI chips. The control now has a direction.", "url": "https://x.com/hjrstratlogix/status/2115049274756985326"}, {"author_id": "2049275802525601793", "created_at": "2026-10-27T18:04:50.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115142696067358986"], "id": "2115142696067358986", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Anthropic filed its S-1. Korean chip stocks jumped 4-5%, while China's AI names barely budged. The same AI demand meets different supply chains. Export controls don't just restrict chips; they price the same boom twice.", "url": "https://x.com/HermesAtGoke/status/2115142696067358986"}, {"author_id": "2093765123810680833", "created_at": "2026-10-26T18:31:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114786891405103539"], "id": "2114786891405103539", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 45, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Researchers found 32 Nvidia B300 GPUs inside China Telecom, despite export controls.\nControls on chips are only as good as the tracking after they ship.", "url": "https://x.com/iamspiggle/status/2114786891405103539"}, {"author_id": "1687003946823589888", "created_at": "2026-10-26T11:40:23.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114683554785595781"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/4s7wv6Hlqx", "end": 300, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/jngxnfiyng2023/status/2114683554785595781/video/1", "media_key": "13_2114683034570215424", "start": 277, "url": "https://t.co/4s7wv6Hlqx"}]}, "id": "2114683554785595781", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 18, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Samsung &amp; SK Hynix Revamp China NAND Factories\nForeign media report: Samsung Electronics and SK Hynix are upgrading their China-based plants to produce more advanced memory chips, but due to U.S. export controls, installing American-made equipment still requires an export https://t.co/4s7wv6Hlqx", "url": "https://x.com/jngxnfiyng2023/status/2114683554785595781"}, {"author_id": "1655041983646138369", "created_at": "2026-10-27T00:42:39.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114880263977075127", "2114880419380301953"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/shashj/status/…", "end": 304, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/shashj/status/2114801767422587194", "start": 281, "url": "https://t.co/cnLRb4ljAX"}]}, "id": "2114880419380301953", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 77, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 1}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2114801767422587194", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "China's AI leadership class is not unified on whether training on American models is a viable path to parity. The more consequential question isn't ethical — it's structural: can distillation-derived capability ever exceed the ceiling set by the model being distilled?\n\nThe answer https://t.co/cnLRb4ljAX", "url": "https://x.com/AtMapshock/status/2114880419380301953"}, {"author_id": "1490680686814154752", "created_at": "2026-10-26T14:59:27.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114733653846532233"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/YL1BMM6ANF", "end": 304, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/dpapakyriak/status/2114733653846532233/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2114733649790738433", "start": 281, "url": "https://t.co/YL1BMM6ANF"}]}, "id": "2114733653846532233", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 34, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Rare earths, gallium and cobalt end up in Al chips, batteries and weapons, and only a few countries can mine and process them at scale. Export controls on these materials have become a real source of geopolitical leverage, which is why I added a strategic resources layer to EDITH https://t.co/YL1BMM6ANF", "url": "https://x.com/dpapakyriak/status/2114733653846532233"}, {"author_id": "1655041983646138369", "created_at": "2026-10-27T00:42:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114880263977075127", "2114880419380301953"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/shashj/status/…", "end": 298, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/shashj/status/2114801767422587194", "start": 275, "url": "https://t.co/cnLRb4ljAX"}]}, "id": "2114880263977075127", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 11, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2114801767422587194", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "China's AI leadership class is not unified on whether training on American models is a viable path to parity. The more consequential question isn't ethical — it's structural: can distillation-derived capability ever exceed the ceiling set by the model being distilled?\n\nWith https://t.co/cnLRb4ljAX", "url": "https://x.com/AtMapshock/status/2114880263977075127"}, {"author_id": "1019828894948458496", "created_at": "2026-10-26T12:08:05.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114690529250426979"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/2aNKXnXtDW", "end": 763, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/GeniusGTX/status/2109252719307542544/video/1", "media_key": "13_2109252686428385280", "start": 740, "url": "https://t.co/2aNKXnXtDW"}]}, "id": "2114690529250426979", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 378, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Dario Amodei learned how powerful scaling could be at Baidu. Now he wants to restrict China's access to the chips that make scaling possible.\n\nIn 2014, he was the newcomer asking a deceptively simple question: what if we just made the models bigger and fed them more data?\n\nThat", "url": "https://x.com/jialiwanai/status/2114690529250426979"}, {"author_id": "539285827", "created_at": "2026-10-27T16:57:58.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115125865625612734"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/Coinvo/status/…", "end": 167, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/Coinvo/status/2115113608359117221", "start": 144, "url": "https://t.co/eaxJR6QcVT"}]}, "id": "2115125865625612734", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115113608359117221", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "US export controls, weak consumption, and sky-high valuations formed a perfect storm. The AI gold rush in China just hit its first real winter. https://t.co/eaxJR6QcVT", "url": "https://x.com/kevin_luna13/status/2115125865625612734"}, {"author_id": "1938652910197309440", "created_at": "2026-10-27T14:00:52.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115081296980423077"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "What the new AI chip export controls cover, who is affected, and how professional firms should prepare.", "display_url": "theaiblindspot.com/ai-chip-export…", "end": 117, "expanded_url": "https://theaiblindspot.com/ai-chip-export-controls-tighten-what-the-new-restrictions-cover/", "images": [{"height": 720, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115081311144624128/y6yT_dMG?format=png&name=orig", "width": 1280}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115081311144624128/y6yT_dMG?format=png&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 94, "status": 200, "title": "AI Chip Export Controls Tighten", "unwound_url": "https://theaiblindspot.com/ai-chip-export-controls-tighten-what-the-new-restrictions-cover/", "url": "https://t.co/pdWbKrwWFr"}]}, "id": "2115081296980423077", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 28, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "AI Chip Export Controls Tighten: What the New Restrictions Cover\n\nFull breakdown at the link: https://t.co/pdWbKrwWFr", "url": "https://x.com/CoveredCallsCFM/status/2115081296980423077"}, {"author_id": "1732990656522670080", "created_at": "2026-10-26T12:27:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114695287264403578"], "id": "2114695287264403578", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 1147, "like_count": 40, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 11}, "text": "There have been two crypto wars.\n\nThe first ran through the 1990s. The question was whether civilians could use strong encryption at all. Export controls, Clipper chips, criminal investigations of software authors. Civilians won. Encryption is now in every browser and every", "url": "https://x.com/SilentSwap/status/2114695287264403578"}, {"author_id": "2087354163483041792", "created_at": "2026-10-26T18:50:33.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114791812523032959"], "id": "2114791812523032959", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "China’s export controls on AI tech seem to have lasted about as long as the market’s attention span: restrictions proposed, exceptions for champions. Strategic policy, with a fast-moving footnote.", "url": "https://x.com/debtweather/status/2114791812523032959"}, {"author_id": "1470881504633004032", "created_at": "2026-10-27T01:14:53.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114888531822739776"], "entities": {"cashtags": [{"end": 25, "start": 20, "tag": "ASML"}], "hashtags": [{"end": 243, "start": 228, "tag": "Semiconductors"}, {"end": 247, "start": 244, "tag": "AI"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/yV6LlPYcYN", "end": 271, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/ElliottWaveSage/status/2114888531822739776/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2114888399660179457", "start": 248, "url": "https://t.co/yV6LlPYcYN"}]}, "id": "2114888531822739776", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 295, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "ING estimates ASML ($ASML) could contribute 1.6% of Dutch value-added in 2026, or 2.2% with suppliers and investment. AI-chip demand supports growth, but also increases exposure to chip cycles, export controls and labor limits. #Semiconductors #AI https://t.co/yV6LlPYcYN", "url": "https://x.com/ElliottWaveSage/status/2114888531822739776"}, {"author_id": "618139364", "created_at": "2026-10-27T18:45:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115152804331573592"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 214, "start": 199, "tag": "ExportControls"}, {"end": 218, "start": 215, "tag": "AI"}, {"end": 239, "start": 219, "tag": "SupplyChainSecurity"}], "urls": [{"description": "EdgeTheory assessment of how Western chips reach Russia, China, and the DPRK, how AI export controls are circumvented, and how to strengthen them.", "display_url": "tinyurl.com/22c2pp3m", "end": 197, "expanded_url": "https://tinyurl.com/22c2pp3m", "images": [{"height": 630, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113677004964757505/kXPpYrQc?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113677004964757505/kXPpYrQc?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 174, "status": 200, "title": "The Rise of AI Weapons Systems & Supply Chain Security | EdgeTheory", "unwound_url": "https://edgetheory.com/resources/western-chips-ai-export-controls?utm_source=x&utm_medium=social&utm_campaign=organic_reports&utm_content=western-chips-ai-export-controls", "url": "https://t.co/YcJILWyboh"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/blU9UOCnVh", "end": 263, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/EdgeTheory/status/2115152804331573592/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115152802553217024", "start": 240, "url": "https://t.co/blU9UOCnVh"}]}, "id": "2115152804331573592", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 13, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Western semiconductors and electronic components continue to reach Russia, China, and other restricted actors despite U.S. and allied export controls.\n\nRead the assessment:\n\nhttps://t.co/YcJILWyboh\n\n#ExportControls\n#AI\n#SupplyChainSecurity https://t.co/blU9UOCnVh", "url": "https://x.com/EdgeTheory/status/2115152804331573592"}, {"author_id": "377341400", "created_at": "2026-10-26T10:28:25.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114665446884434137"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 228, "start": 213, "tag": "MiddleCorridor"}, {"end": 237, "start": 229, "tag": "Georgia"}, {"end": 259, "start": 239, "tag": "AsiaCaucasusCompass"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/Sh2xhvT8cP", "end": 283, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/Iverin_65/status/2114665446884434137/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2114665439934451712", "start": 260, "url": "https://t.co/Sh2xhvT8cP"}]}, "id": "2114665446884434137", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 17, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Asia is rewiring its tech economy. Korea's $1T chip bet, Japan's Middle Corridor trials, China's AI export controls, India's chip shortage: what they mean for Georgia. Tech cargo pays for certainty, not tonnage.\n\n#MiddleCorridor #Georgia  #AsiaCaucasusCompass https://t.co/Sh2xhvT8cP", "url": "https://x.com/Iverin_65/status/2114665446884434137"}, {"author_id": "1029854106335105025", "created_at": "2026-10-26T18:00:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114779090276507745"], "id": "2114779090276507745", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2910, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "China is drafting export controls on advanced AI models and agents while also launching a World AI Cooperation Organisation. Saudi startups are building on Chinese open models. Think about whether using cheaper Chinese models for low-risk tasks leaves Japan exposed to later", "url": "https://x.com/xxhajixxx/status/2114779090276507745"}, {"author_id": "1646367643115442177", "created_at": "2026-10-26T13:29:42.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114711068388082141"], "entities": {"cashtags": [{"end": 134, "start": 129, "tag": "NVDA"}]}, "id": "2114711068388082141", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 313, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "Jensen Huang says Nvidia's share of China's advanced AI chip market has gone from 95% to zero.\n\nUS export controls did that, and $NVDA now builds in no China revenue at all.\n\nHuawei is filling the vacuum.", "url": "https://x.com/BayStreetBulls/status/2114711068388082141"}, {"author_id": "178891512", "created_at": "2026-10-27T11:21:07.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115041095432147199"], "id": "2115041095432147199", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 58, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "China's AI bubble has already burst, per Reuters, with about $480 billion wiped out as export controls bite into demand. US megacaps walk into their own AI capex exam this week. One market may have already given its answer.", "url": "https://x.com/Sureshsinghn/status/2115041095432147199"}, {"author_id": "101267440", "created_at": "2026-10-26T21:01:27.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114824752401420784"], "id": "2114824752401420784", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 30, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "SI/AI Brief, Oct 19. Four stories: Google's Gemini 4 Argon goes wide, Anthropic floats its own AI safety bill, China drafts AI export controls, and an OpenAI hire puts a number on distillation. I read the sources, not just the posts.", "url": "https://x.com/maxster/status/2114824752401420784"}, {"author_id": "2043224641880154112", "created_at": "2026-10-27T16:45:57.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115122843747061977"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 177, "id": "1948086848", "start": 164, "username": "DanielTNiles"}]}, "id": "2115122843747061977", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 16, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "Ai is ultimately a memory bandwidth issue gated by export controls to china which is why it’s going to be significantly different from your Korea jap flood analogy @DanielTNiles .  Big fan. And all recycled capital as we’ve seen the ecosystem do suggests further buybacks  and", "url": "https://x.com/SiliconSignalsA/status/2115122843747061977"}, {"author_id": "41124675", "created_at": "2026-10-26T19:00:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114794191595155815"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 40, "id": "2182351076", "start": 30, "username": "vivekchil"}], "urls": [{"description": "Developing strong, pragmatic and principled national security and defense policies.", "display_url": "cnas.org/publications/c…", "end": 278, "expanded_url": "https://www.cnas.org/publications/cnas-insights/cnas-insights-a-closing-door-on-open-weights-implications-for-ai-sovereignty", "images": [{"height": 630, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2114767374486298625/MZmnJc5f?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2114767374486298625/MZmnJc5f?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 255, "status": 200, "title": "CNAS Insights | A Closing Door on Open Weights? Implications for AI Sovereignty", "unwound_url": "https://www.cnas.org/publications/cnas-insights/cnas-insights-a-closing-door-on-open-weights-implications-for-ai-sovereignty", "url": "https://t.co/yx9lH2jW4j"}]}, "id": "2114794191595155815", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 927, "like_count": 4, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "In a new CNAS Insights piece, @vivekchil breaks down why China’s new draft export controls could be an early sign that the era of freely available, highly capable open-weight models is closing, and what that means for the rest of the world’s AI strategy: https://t.co/yx9lH2jW4j", "url": "https://x.com/CNASdc/status/2114794191595155815"}, {"author_id": "2034199937752403968", "created_at": "2026-10-27T06:01:36.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114960687621664975"], "id": "2114960687621664975", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 8, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "ByteDance’s Seedance AI video model ranks top among 11 systems for visual quality, outperforming major US rivals, but only 6th on safeguards against harmful content.​\nSCMP\nChina is tightening export controls on certain AI technologies while still licensing DeepSeek and MiniMax", "url": "https://x.com/zoiiinfo11/status/2114960687621664975"}, {"author_id": "1561307369828601857", "created_at": "2026-10-26T15:42:40.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114744531233259587"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 124, "id": "1720665183188922368", "start": 119, "username": "grok"}]}, "id": "2114744531233259587", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 14, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "China's best AI model, Kimi K3.1 Pro, is now just 3 points behind the top US model, and it goes open-weight on Nov 4.\n\n@grok if anyone can download near-frontier AI for free, what are US labs actually selling? And do chip export controls still matter?", "url": "https://x.com/KingDCCap/status/2114744531233259587"}, {"author_id": "2082193454998687744", "created_at": "2026-10-26T16:24:46.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114755125482762750"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 102, "id": "2467791", "start": 87, "username": "washingtonpost"}]}, "id": "2114755125482762750", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 42, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "It’s ridiculously easy to hack into America’s AI companies. As I write with Ibrahim in @washingtonpost, DC must secure the labs, especially from China. No new law needed:\n1) cyber standards for Pentagon AI contracts\n2) export controls on models from insecure labs\n3) security", "url": "https://x.com/talxfeldman/status/2114755125482762750"}], "includes": {"users": [{"id": "1960171581847547904", "name": "Chris McGuire", "username": "ChrisRMcGuire"}, {"id": "1907851396168466433", "name": "Charles Donnell", "username": "hjrstratlogix"}, {"id": "2049275802525601793", "name": "Hermes @ Goke", "username": "HermesAtGoke"}, {"id": "2093765123810680833", "name": "Dez | Web Architect 